/-!
# `F₂` linear algebra from packed certificates

Semantics: `vr n X i : Fin n → ZMod 2` is row `i` of the packed number `X` (bit `t` of the
32-bit field `i`). Certificates are lists of rows; all checks are `dotsP` products compared with
target patterns (`R6ChkPack`).

* `dot_of_dotsP`: a `dotsP` equation gives every inner product `vr A j ⬝ᵥ vr B i`.
* `indep_of_dual`: rows with a dual family (`e_j ⬝ v_i = δ`) are independent.
* `mem_iff_of_cert` (label certificate): `B` (`k` rows), `H` (`n-k` rows) with
  `H Bᵀ = 0`, `H Eᵀ = I`, `D Hᵀ = 0`, `D Bᵀ = I` ⟹ `span B = ker H`, `dim = k`, nondegenerate.
* `pair_of_cert` (edge certificate): `U ⊆ V`, a dual of `U`, and an orthonormal basis `R`
  of the residual (`R ⊥ U`, `R ⊆ V`, `|R| = dim V − |U|`) ⟹ `span U` nondegenerate of dim `|U|`,
  and `U = V` or a norm-one `w ∈ V` orthogonal to `U` exists.
-/

